1200 GOSUB 6320:BM$="Man: This is all thanks to your dark arts, Master Hroth. The lands have\never been more fertile. The people are eternally grateful to you.":GOSUB 5100
1210 BM$="Apparently, the man who looked like an older David was called Hroth.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1220 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Hroth: No need to be modest, Lafir. My dark arts merely laid the\groundwork; everything else was your work.":GOSUB 5100
1230 BM$="Lafir, the other man, seemed to be around 80 years old. He acted like some\sort of guardian to Hroth, the king.":GOSUB 5100
1240 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Hroth: I hope the people of the North are faring well. I'd like to send them\some of our crops.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1250 GOSUB 6320:BM$="Lafir: I'm afraid the King of the North would refuse your assistance. As\long as he and his family can live a life of luxury, he doesn't care if his\people starve to death.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1260 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Hroth: Is there truly nothing we can do to save them?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1270 GOSUB 6320:BM$="Lafir: My liege, I ask you to forget about the people of the North. The King\of the North would take any action as a personal insult. If he were to\declare war, we wouldn't be able to defend ourselves.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1280 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Hroth: A king should strive to bring joy to his people. I wish the King of the\North understood that.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1290 GOSUB 6320:BM$="Lafir: He already accuses you of being a Devil King who uses the dark arts\for his own gain. I beg you sire, do not stir the hornet's nest any further.":GOSUB 5100
1335 GOSUB 6900:COMMON FO:GOSUB 6200:BM$="Then, Hroth vanished, and the rest of the scenery followed.":GOSUB 5100
1340 GOSUB 6210:BM$="David: ...That wasn't a dream. I was conscious the entire time, I can feel it.\Why am I so tired...?":GOSUB 5100
1345 BM$="David tried to summon the scene again, but he was too tired to focus. Soon\after, he fell asleep.":GOSUB 5100
